### AgentCore Runtime requires session ids of at least 33 characters, so the
### examples use ids of that length even locally.

### Health check (AgentCore /ping contract)
GET http://localhost:8080/ping

### First turn — introduce yourself (memory will store this)
POST http://localhost:8080/invocations
Content-Type: application/json
X-Amzn-Bedrock-AgentCore-Runtime-Session-Id: demo-session-0000000000000000000001

{
  "prompt": "Hi, I'm Maya. I'm planning a trip from Seattle to Tokyo next month and I prefer window seats."
}

### Second turn — the agent should remember Maya, plan, and call tools
POST http://localhost:8080/invocations
Content-Type: application/json
X-Amzn-Bedrock-AgentCore-Runtime-Session-Id: demo-session-0000000000000000000001

{
  "prompt": "What's the weather like at my destination, and roughly what will the flight cost?"
}

### Third turn — verify recall of the earlier preference
POST http://localhost:8080/invocations
Content-Type: application/json
X-Amzn-Bedrock-AgentCore-Runtime-Session-Id: demo-session-0000000000000000000001

{
  "prompt": "Remind me what seating preference I mentioned earlier."
}
